OL,3,GNEWSAGet set, ready, go! Great North
OL,4,ARun weekend begins
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Great North Run (GNR) returns to
OL,7,FTyneside this weekend, with 63,000
OL,8,Frunners taking part in the world's
OL,9,Fbiggest half marathon on Sunday.
OL,11,FSaturday's Mini and Junior events on
OL,12,FNewcastle's Quayside are in their 40th
OL,13,Fyear and see 13,000 young people take
OL,14,Fon courses ranging from 50m (164ft) to
OL,15,F4km (2.5 miles).
OL,17,FGladiators Alex Gray (Apollo), Emily
OL,18,FSteel (Dynamite) and Matty Campbell
OL,19,F(Bionic) are ringing Saturday's
OL,20,Fstarters' bell alongside GNR mascot
OL,21,FTyney the Tortoise, while Newcastle
OL,22,Fcaptain Dan Burn is Sunday's starter.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,395,390,260,160,0,100
